# beam4pm-pro-entitlement-pack introduces NO vocabulary of its own.
#
# Every template here (beam4pm_entitlement.{erl,ex}.tmpl,
# beam4pm_billing.{erl,ex}.tmpl, and their test siblings) queries
# bpm:RecordType / bpm:Field directly -- the exact same vocabulary
# beam4pm-process-model-pack already declares (bpm:recordName, bpm:recordDoc,
# bpm:hasField, bpm:fieldName, bpm:fieldType, bpm:fieldDoc, bpm:fieldRequired,
# bpm:fieldOrder). A consumer project mints its own entitlement_event /
# entitlement_state / usage_event / billing_reconciliation bpm:RecordType
# individuals (under the consumer's own namespace, in the consumer's own
# ontology fragment), and these templates render real structs/records plus
# the reconcile_entitlement/2 and reconcile_billing/reconcile/4 algorithms
# from that admitted graph -- the same schema-only contract
# beam4pm-pro-infra-pack already uses for its own vocabulary.
#
# This file ships zero individuals AND zero new classes/properties -- it
# exists only so tooling that expects every pack directory to carry an
# ontology.ttl finds one, and so this decision is documented at the one
# place someone extending this pack would look first.
